        <Options>
            <Main applyHouseholdOperatingConditions="false" applyReducedOperatingConditions="false" atypicalElectricalLoads="false" waterConservation="false" referenceHouse="false">
                <Vermiculite code="1">
                    <English>Unknown</English>
                    <French>Inconnu</French>
                </Vermiculite>
            </Main>
            <RURComments xml:space="preserve">
                <airSeal>This house has a lot of air leaks as we saw with the blower door test. You must deal with these air leaks as soon as possible. The areas to focus on are where the new and old units are attached, between the 2 original units. The ceiling above the electrical panel and any cracks in the drywall. Around the windows and exterior electrical outlets as well as the weather stripping on the doors. </airSeal>
                <ceilings>Adding insulation to the ceiling won't result in much savings but would be a good opportunity to focuson air sealing in the ceiling.</ceilings>
                <foundation>Adding insulation under the floor wouldn't save a significant amount but air sealing could be done in the crawlspace at the ame time. Upgrading by at least R-20 would also be eligible for a Good Energy Rebate. </foundation>
                <windows>The windows where you spend the most time should be upgraded to increase the comfort in the home. Windows are eligible for a Good Energy rebate.</windows>
            </RURComments>
        </Options>
